parameters.text:
=Compare the following data and identify any changes:

=== PREVIOUS DATA (from Google Sheet) ===
Company: {{ $('Historical Data').item.json['Company Name'] }}
URL: {{ $('Historical Data').item.json.URL }}
Summary: {{ $json.Summary }}

=== CURRENT DATA (newly extracted) ===
Company: {{ $('Data Summarization Agent').item.json.output.company_name }}
URL: {{ $('Data Summarization Agent').item.json.output.website_url }}
Summary: Features: {{ $('Data Summarization Agent').item.json.output.features_summary }}
Pricing Detail:{{ $('Data Summarization Agent').item.json.output.pricing_summary }}
Total plans:{{ $('Data Summarization Agent').item.json.output.total_plans }}

Task:
1. Compare both datasets carefully
2. Identify ALL changes (pricing, plans, features)
3. Generate a SHORT summary (1-2 lines, max 150 characters)
4. Set changes_detected to true if ANY change found, false otherwise
5. If no changes, return empty string "" for change_summary

Focus on:
- Price changes (exact amounts)
- Plan count changes
- New/removed plans
- New/removed features

Return ONLY valid JSON matching the schema.

parameters.inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "changes_detected": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "True if any changes found, false if no changes"
    },
    "change_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "One or two line summary of changes (max 150 characters). Empty string if no changes."
    }
  },
  "required": ["changes_detected", "change_summary"]
}

parameters.jsCode:
// Extract all companies with their changes
const allData = [];

items.forEach(item => {
  if (item.json.data && Array.isArray(item.json.data)) {
    item.json.data.forEach(dataItem => {
      allData.push({
        companyName: dataItem['Company Name'],
        changesDetect: dataItem['Changes Detect']
      });
    });
  }
});

// Return as single output
return [{ json: { companies: allData } }];

